Deviation from the plan's Scope (accepted by plan amendment 2, commit 434250c, plan Status)
  - The plan's Scope names one application start. POST /api/rag/evaluate accepts only hybrid, rerank and trace per call
    (RetrievalEvaluationController.evaluate: @RequestParam hybrid, rerank, trace); candidate count, rerank-candidates and rerank-timeout-ms are
    application properties. So each run had its own application start with RAG_* environment variables (observed: the controller source). The
    property diff (property-diff.txt) compares the recorded properties the three starts stored; rerank-timeout-ms and max-length are not recorded
    (logged values below).
  - Each start made one warm-up call (POST /api/rag/retrieve, as in the counterpart procedure; amendment 2 names it). Embedding calls: 168 evaluation
    (runs a, b, c, and the repeat of c) + 4 warm-up, plus 1 warm-up of the aborted attempt P1: 173 in total (derived: count of "Query embedding
    completed" over the five app.log files, 1 + 43 + 43 + 43 + 43).
  - Amendment 2 allows run c to be repeated once after its rerank fallback, as a new snapshot, with run c kept committed and labelled: see "Run c repeat".

Per-run procedure (a scratch script, run.sh, ran these commands in this order)
  1. Run shell: cd <project>; set -a; source .env; set +a; export SERVER_PORT=8081 INTEGRATION_ACCESS_TOKEN=<42-character random hex token, openssl rand
     -hex 21, not recorded> RAG_CROSS_ENCODER_ENABLED=true plus the run's overrides; env | grep -E '^(RAG_[A-Z0-9_]*|RECOMMENDATION_ENABLED|OUTCOMES_ENABLED|
     IBKR_ENABLED|WATCHLIST_ENABLED|SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE|SERVER_PORT)=' printed (per run below); lsof on 8081 -> 0 listeners before every start.
  2. CPU sharing wait: ps -ax -o pid=,args= filtered on surefire|spring-boot:run|StockRecommendationEngineApplication, excluding this run's own mvnw and
     application pids; poll every 30 s, up to 30 minutes; before the app start and before the evaluate call.
  3. nohup ./mvnw -q -o spring-boot:run > app.log 2>&1 &; wait for "Started StockRecommendationEngineApplication"; the "Cross-encoder loaded" line.
  4. Warm-up: curl -X POST http://localhost:8081/api/rag/retrieve -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>" -H 'Content-Type: application/json'
       -d '{"ticker":"NVDA","query":"What was NVIDIA gross margin in fiscal 2026?","rerank":true}'
  5. CPU sharing wait, sysctl -n vm.loadavg, curl --max-time 1200 -X POST "http://localhost:8081/api/rag/evaluate?<query>" -H "Authorization: Bearer <token>".
  6. curl GET /api/rag/evaluate/<id> and GET /api/rag/evaluate/<id>/evidence (HTTP status and bytes below).
  7. docker exec -i trading-postgres sh -c 'psql -U "$POSTGRES_USER" -d "$POSTGRES_DB" -tA -c "select row_to_json(e) from retrieval_evaluations e where id = <id>"'
     -> snapshot-<id>-<run>.json (the single output line with its newline, unaltered).
  8. evidence-<id>.json: the fetched evidence body with whitespace (space, tab, CR, LF) outside JSON strings removed, one line plus a newline; a scratch
     script parsed both texts with every number and constant kept as its written text and printed parses_equal_numbers_as_written=True for each.
  9. grep -E 'Cross-encoder scoring completed|Reranking failed|Retrieval evaluation stored|WARN|ERROR' app.log -> scoring-<id>.txt.
  10. Stop: kill the port-8081 listener JVM by pid; 5 s later the mvnw pid if alive; pkill -f spring-boot:run; then lsof on 8081, both pids, and
      pgrep -f spring-boot:run checked (per run below). app.log ends with Maven's "[ERROR] Failed to execute goal ... spring-boot-maven-plugin:4.1.1:run"
      help lines, written after the kill (observed, as in the counterpart runs).

